---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Resume — Luna Puvilland"
  description="Luna Puvilland — computer engineering undergrad at McGill. C&DH lead for the Orbital CubeSat, infrastructure and security."
>
  <div class="wrap area no-print">
    <p class="area__kicker">The formal record</p>
    <h1 class="area__title">Resume</h1>
    <p class="area__sub">The same facts as the rest of the site, formatted for people who ask for a PDF.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap paper-wrap">
    <div class="paper__actions no-print">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" id="print-resume"><span class="soul" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Print / save as PDF ↓
      </button>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:luna@craftcat.dev">Email</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/lpuv" rel="me">GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>

    <article class="paper">
      <header class="paper__head">
        <div>
          <h2 class="paper__name">Luna Sonlam Puvilland</h2>
          <p class="paper__role">Computer Engineering · McGill University · Class of 2029</p>
        </div>
        <div class="paper__contact">
          <a href="mailto:luna@craftcat.dev">luna@craftcat.dev</a><br />
          <a href="https://github.com/lpuv">github.com/lpuv</a><br />
          Montréal, QC
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
          Computer engineering student at McGill, C&amp;DH lead for the Orbital CubeSat, and
          infrastructure volunteer at Fedora. I build systems that stay up, and I take old
          software apart to see how it breaks. Security work is the other half, mostly CTFs and
          red-team labs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>B.Eng. Computer Engineering — McGill University</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">Class of 2029</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Montréal, QC · GPA 3.4</span>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>IB Diploma — Eagle Rock High School</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">2024 — 2025</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Los Angeles, CA</span>
          <p class="entry__note">
            AP Computer Science A (5), French (5), Physics A (4), Calculus AB (4), Chemistry (4).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Experience</h2>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>Command and Data Handling Lead — McGill Rocket Team: CubeSat Division</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">Sep 2025 — present</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">McGill University</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Lead the C&amp;DH division for McGill's Orbital CubeSat.</li>
            <li>Own the firmware and software stack on the TMS570LS0714PZQ core MCU.</li>
            <li>
              Direct data intake from auxiliary systems and manage the division's DevOps
              workflows.
            </li>
            <li>Program a barebones operating system for the onboard TI microcontroller.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>Software Engineering Intern — Cerbrec Inc.</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">May 2025 — Jul 2025</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Graphbook</span>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Translated operations from shared libraries such as Scikit into Graphbook's
              custom language and interface.
            </li>
            <li>
              Implemented diagonalization, covariance matrix calculation, and dataset
              standardization.
            </li>
            <li>Integrated the Principal Component Analysis algorithm.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>Infrastructure Volunteer &amp; Packager — Fedora Project</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">Dec 2021 — present</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Open source</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Package software tools and submit them to official Fedora repositories.</li>
            <li>Resolve tickets and manage project resources in the Ansible-based infrastructure.</li>
            <li>Deploy applications to project servers using Kubernetes and OpenShift.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>IT Volunteer — Eagle Rock High School</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">Sep 2024 — May 2025</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Los Angeles, CA</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Built an asset management website for the IT office's Chromebook checkout process.</li>
            <li>Implemented student ID scanning and automated SMS reminders for overdue assets.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__line">
            <h3>Penetration Testing &amp; Systems Admin — TryHackMe / HackTheBox</h3>
            <span class="entry__meta">Dec 2017 — present</span>
          </div>
          <span class="entry__org">Self-directed</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Completed the Red Teamer Capstone against a simulated 17-host corporate network.</li>
            <li>Top 1% of TryHackMe users; authored challenges for TryHackMe and McGill's CTF.</li>
            <li>
              Administer Linux and Unix systems with a focus on virtualized applications and
              simulated high-availability Kubernetes environments.
            </li>
            <li>Configure and integrate servers with Ansible in containers, deploying via OpenShift.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
        <table class="spec--paper">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Languages</th>
              <td>Python, C, C++, JavaScript, Java, Swift, Node.js</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Infrastructure</th>
              <td>
                Linux, Kubernetes, Ansible, OpenShift, Proxmox, NixOS, Docker, Git, Azure DevOps,
                Jira
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Embedded</th>
              <td>TMS570, JTAG debugging, oscilloscopes, MATLAB/Simulink</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Security</th>
              <td>Penetration testing, CTF, vulnerability research, least-privilege design</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Selected Projects</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Orbital CubeSat C&amp;DH</strong> — Firmware and software stack for the
            TMS570 onboard computer.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>nix-lab</strong> — Single-flake NixOS homelab; every host reproducible, every
            change reversible.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>grimoire</strong> — Blood on the Clocktower bot for Discord, replacing
            Bureaucrat.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CVE-2012-2982</strong> — End-to-end reproduction and exploit of a Webmin
            authenticated RCE.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>evil-tetris</strong> — A deliberately hostile Tetris clone in Godot.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.8rem;">
          <a href="/systems">Full system records →</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Awards</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>1st Place, CTF Introduction Course — DEF CON 31 (2023).</li>
          <li>Enigma Award — US Space and Rocket Center Cyber Camp (Jun 2023).</li>
          <li>Capstone Awards — TryHackMe (2021–2023).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="paper__foot">
        Montréal, QC · luna@craftcat.dev · github.com/lpuv
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  document.getElementById('print-resume')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
</script>
